## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to build a scalable, privacy-preserving ML pipeline that composes multiple AWS services (S3, Step Functions, Lambda, SageMaker) with governance and observability.

## Key Concepts

- Event-driven pipelines with S3 triggers
- Step Functions coordinating Lambda and SageMaker
- PII redaction in Lambda
- SageMaker inference integration for sentiment and topics
- Data governance: KMS encryption, least-privilege IAM, auditing
- Reliability: DLQ, retries, monitoring, cost controls

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lambda pseudocode for redacting PII from JSON input
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const data = JSON.parse(event.body || '{}');
  if (data.email) data.email = '[REDACTED]';
  if (data.phone) data.phone = '[REDACTED]';
  return { redacted: true, data };
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate redaction quality and model bias at scale?
- What strategies ensure latency targets under burst traffic?
- How would you enforce data-retention policies and revocation requests across services?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end understanding of an AWS-based AI data flow, including extraction, NLP, storage, and indexing, plus privacy and cost controls.

## Key Concepts
- Event-driven design with S3, Lambda, Textract, Comprehend, DynamoDB
- IAM least privilege and KMS encryption
- Observability: DLQ, retries, CloudWatch
- Data governance: PII detection, versioning guidance

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Lambda handler sketch
exports.handler = async (evt) => {
  const s3Key = evt.Records[0].s3.object.key;
  const text = await textract.extractText(s3Key);
  const topics = await comprehend.classify(text);
  const pii = comprehend.detectPII(text);
  await s3.writeJSON(text, s3Key.replace('input','output'));
  await dynamo.upsert({ designId, s3Key, transcriptKey: '...', topics, piiFlag: pii > 0, timestamp: Date.now()});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale for 10k+ files/day?
- How would you validate privacy policies and redact data consistently?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design end-to-end data pipelines in AWS using serverless components, data cataloging, and lightweight ETL operations while considering security, privacy, and cost optimization.

## Key Concepts
- S3 event triggers and Lambda orchestration
- AWS Glue Data Catalog and crawlers for schema inference
- Lightweight ETL transformations in Lambda (normalization, data validation)
- DynamoDB indexing with upsert operations for idempotency
- IAM roles with least-privilege access
- Encryption at rest (SSE-KMS) and in transit (TLS)
- S3 access logs for audit trails
- Retry mechanisms and dead-letter queues for error handling
- Cost considerations: Lambda invocation duration, Glue crawler runtime, S3 storage, and DynamoDB read/write capacity

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Lambda handler invoking Glue and orchestrating ETL
const { GlueClient, StartCrawlerCommand } = require('@aws-sdk/client-glue');
const { S3Client, PutObjectCommand } = require('@aws-sdk/client-s3');
const { DynamoDBClient, PutItemCommand } = require('@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb');

exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const s3Record = event.Records[0].s3;
  const bucket = s3Record.bucket.name;
  const key = decodeURIComponent(s3Record.object.key.replace(/\+/g, ' '));

  const glue = new GlueClient({});
  await glue.send(new StartCrawlerCommand({ Name: 'csv-crawler' }));

  // ETL: Normalize headers, drop rows with missing values
  const cleanedData = await processCSV(bucket, key);

  const s3 = new S3Client({});
  await s3.send(new PutObjectCommand({
    Bucket: bucket,
    Key: `cleaned/${key}`,
    Body: cleanedData,
    ServerSideEncryption: 'aws:kms'
  }));

  const dynamo = new DynamoDBClient({});
  await dynamo.send(new PutItemCommand({
    TableName: 'file-index',
    Item: {
      fileId: { S: key },
      s3Key: { S: key },
      rowCount: { N: '100' },
      columnCount: { N: '5' },
      status: { S: 'COMPLETED' }
    }
  }));
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement retries and idempotency to avoid reprocessing on failures?
- What cost optimization strategies would you apply for a high-volume pipeline?
- How would you handle schema evolution if the CSV structure changes over time?
